(RADIOLOGY TERMINOLOGY - MEDICAL REFERENCE) Tj
0 -30 Td
(=========================================) Tj
0 -40 Td
(COMMON IMAGING MODALITIES) Tj
0 -25 Td
(1. X-RAY \(RADIOGRAPHY\)) Tj
0 -15 Td
(   - Uses ionizing radiation to create images) Tj
0 -15 Td
(   - Best for: Bones, chest, dental imaging) Tj
0 -15 Td
(   - Common findings: Fractures, pneumonia, tumors) Tj
0 -25 Td
(2. CT SCAN \(COMPUTED TOMOGRAPHY\)) Tj
0 -15 Td
(   - Cross-sectional imaging using X-rays) Tj
0 -15 Td
(   - Best for: Detailed organ visualization, trauma) Tj
0 -15 Td
(   - Terms: Hypodense \(darker\), Hyperdense \(brighter\)) Tj
0 -25 Td
(3. MRI \(MAGNETIC RESONANCE IMAGING\)) Tj
0 -15 Td
(   - Uses magnetic fields and radio waves) Tj
0 -15 Td
(   - Best for: Soft tissues, brain, spinal cord) Tj
0 -15 Td
(   - No ionizing radiation) Tj
0 -25 Td
(4. ULTRASOUND) Tj
0 -15 Td
(   - Uses high-frequency sound waves) Tj
0 -15 Td
(   - Best for: Pregnancy, abdominal organs, blood flow) Tj
0 -15 Td
(   - Real-time imaging, safe and non-invasive) Tj
0 -30 Td
(COMMON RADIOLOGY TERMS) Tj
0 -20 Td
(- Opacity: Area that blocks X-rays \(appears white\)) Tj
0 -15 Td
(- Lucency: Area that allows X-rays through \(appears dark\)) Tj
0 -15 Td
(- Consolidation: Filling of airspaces in lungs) Tj
0 -15 Td
(- Atelectasis: Collapsed or airless lung) Tj
0 -15 Td
(- Effusion: Fluid collection \(pleural, pericardial\)) Tj
0 -15 Td
(- Mass: Abnormal tissue growth) Tj
0 -15 Td
(- Nodule: Small rounded lesion) Tj
0 -15 Td
(- Calcification: Calcium deposits in tissue) Tj
0 -30 Td
(CHEST X-RAY FINDINGS) Tj
0 -20 Td
(- Cardiomegaly: Enlarged heart) Tj
0 -15 Td
(- Pneumothorax: Air in pleural space) Tj
0 -15 Td
(- Infiltrate: Abnormal substance in lung tissue) Tj
0 -15 Td
(- Fibrosis: Scarring of lung tissue) Tj
0 -30 Td
(Note: Always correlate imaging with clinical findings.) Tj
